after months of waiting and speculation  at the full trailer for the eighth and  final season of Game of Thrones has  finally arrived ahead of the premiere on  April 14th from dragons at Winterfell  two significant glasses of wine here are  some small details you may have missed  Greyjoy family infighting took up a lot  of time in the seventh season good  things happened for Theon who reclaimed  his name after being tortured by Ramsay  Bolton  but Yara his formidable older sister was  captured and held hostage by conniving  uncle Johan hoping to provoke Theon  interet ally ating Euron currently holds  all the power in the situation with his  fleet having destroyed yara ships though  he seems to serve Cersei it's more  likely that he's simply looking out for  his own interests it's clear that at  least one Greyjoy ship is on the move in  the new trailer where a ship bearing the  Greyjoy's sigil is seen stuffed with an  entire army the leader of the ship is  sporting gold armor and slicked back  blond hair whoever it is it's the sure  sign that we haven't seen the last of  the Greyjoy family conflict in the final  moments of season 7 the night king used  his new ice dragon to demolish the wall  setting up an intense scenario for the  final season viewers were also concerned  about the fate of two characters who  were guarding the wall when it fell  tormund and beric Dondarrion it's a long  way down  crows keep telling me I'll get used to  it fun favorite tormund has been winning  over audiences for years two viewers  were devastated by the possibility of  his death but beric is known for  surviving almost anything through red  magic so it seemed possible that he  could still be alive  thankfully the trailer gave anxious fans  a glimpse of both torment and barek  flaming sword and all the most explosive  secret revealed during the sixth season  was that Jon Snow is not Ned Stark's  illegitimate son but actually Aegon  Targaryen rightful heir to the Iron  Throne  he's also the nephew to the nearest  Targaryen with whom he has recently  struck up a new problematic romance we  don't choose India currently the lovers  remain blissfully ignorant to their  family ties and the only characters with  any concrete knowledge of John's lineage  a bran stark and Sam Tali who haven't  got a chance to tell him yet the trailer  has a few shots hinting at when John and  Daenerys might find out about each other  there's a moment between the two in the  crypts of Winterfell where John's mother  Liana is buried as well as a moment with  the two of them approaching the Dragons  together which might mean John is taking  a ride on one this season John can also  be seen lingering in the godswood a  place that's been very important to the  stark family there's also a shot of  salmon bran looking furtively at someone  off screen which could be the moment  just before they break the news to John  about his new girlfriend the trailer  shows both of Daenerys is remaining  dragons arriving at Winterfell  stunning Sansa as she stands on the  ramparts fans already knew that the  dragons would return for the final  season as they will play an instrumental  part in the war against the White  Walkers  but bazarian Daenerys s third dragon who  fell during a battle with the night King  is conspicuously absent from the trailer  there's a lot of questions surrounding  vissarion's return like whether or not  Daenerys will be able to control him or  if he might return to his former self in  enemy hands he's a game changer and  leaving him out of the trailer feels  significance throughout Game of Thrones  Gendry has remained an enigma as one of  the only surviving Buster's of King  Robert Baratheon  he has been hunted and in hiding for  most of the series but though he has a  significant claim to the Iron Throne he  doesn't seem to want control of the  Seven Kingdoms as an apprentice  blacksmith he seems more concerned with  surviving than rolling  gendry's long absence was resolved in  season seven with  reveal that he's still working as a  blacksmith in the season 8 trailer he  seems to be forging swords which is  important in the lead-up to the final  battle with the White Walkers on the  move Westeros needs Valyrian steel  swords more than ever and Gendry may be  just the man for the job  audiences see two glimpses of Cersei  Lannister during the trailer and they  couldn't be more different  first she's standing triumphantly on the  shores of King's Landing flanked by the  sycophantic Coburn and her undead  bodyguard she looks completely in  control but in her next shots she's  alone in a quiet throne room holding a  glass of wine and seemingly on the verge  of tears last time we saw Cersei  clutching wine on the Iron Throne  it was drawing season two's Blackwater  when she thought the city was about to  fall so to mimic that moment seem  significant also last season saw her  shock her family by revealing that she  was pregnant with Jamie's baby after the  reveal as she began to conspicuously  decline alcohol so we have to wonder  what happens to make Cersei pick up the  bottle again one of the longest-running  couples of the entire show came to an  apparent end during the seventh season  when Jaime Lannister left his sister  behind to help protect Westeros he's  disgusted that Cersei would choose to  stay out of the fight against the White  Walkers so he leaves King's Landing  apparently heading to Winterfell to join  his brother Tyrion against Circe's  wishes even though there's still time  for Jamie to return to his sister side  he seems to be sticking to his guns and  the trailer but there was not revealed  where he is  fans can guess that he may have arrived  at Winterfell as he tells an unseen  character that he promised to fight for  the living not just the Lannisters  since Jamie is seen elsewhere in the  trailer bloodied and fighting at a  castle that maybe Winterfell it seems  like he may just turn against Cersei  after all throughout the trailer  glimpses of battles pop up here and  there but thanks to plenty of fire and  smoke it's still unconfirmed where those  particular scenes take place however in  the final shot of the trailer viewers  clearly see Daenerys as army of  unsullied alongside Brienne of Tarth her  loyal Squire Podrick Payne and an  heiress his closest advisor Jorah  Mormont waiting in front of Winterfell  is a ghostly horse's legs quietly take a  step towards them indicating the fate of  Westeros may come down to a massive  battle at Winterfell  where the series introduced us to its  world years ago we hope they've got  enough for Larry and Steele we know  Brienne has a Valyrian sword but the  rest of the army could be woefully  underprepared hope somebody brought the  Dragons check out one of our newest  videos right here plus even more looper  videos about your favorite stuff are  coming soon subscribe to our YouTube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  [Music]
 

